Subject: [flux] Do not warn about missing Google API keys

The bar reads "Google API keys are missing. Some functionality of Chromium
will be disabled." - on first run, on every profile, permanently. It is wrong
three times over in this fork: the keys are missing on purpose, nothing it
warns about is functionality Flux uses, and it names Chromium to a user who
installed Flux.

dev.gn already says outright that without the keys "sync, safe-browsing,
geolocation and translate are inert". That is a description of the intended
build, not a degraded one. An infobar that cannot be acted on and will never
go away is worse than no infobar.

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/startup/infobar_utils.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/startup/infobar_utils.cc
@@ -185,9 +185,17 @@
   infobars::ContentInfoBarManager* infobar_manager =
       infobars::ContentInfoBarManager::FromWebContents(web_contents);
 
-  if (!google_apis::HasAPIKeyConfigured()) {
-    GoogleApiKeysInfoBarDelegate::Create(infobar_manager);
-  }
+  // Flux deliberately ships no Google API keys, so Chromium's warning about
+  // them is permanent, unactionable, and names a product the user did not
+  // install. Everything it refers to - sync, Safe Browsing lookups,
+  // geolocation, translate - is a Google service this browser does not use;
+  // its own account state lives in the connector store. Removed outright
+  // rather than made conditional, because there is no configuration of this
+  // fork in which showing it would be right.
+  //
+  // Upstream:
+  //   if (!google_apis::HasAPIKeyConfigured())
+  //     GoogleApiKeysInfoBarDelegate::Create(infobar_manager);
 
   if (ObsoleteSystem::IsObsoleteNowOrSoon()) {
     PrefService* local_state = g_browser_process->local_state();
